  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed two storey side extension, by reason of its excessive width and the absence of a 1m set back from the common boundary with No. 9 Ambleside Crescent, would result in a visually incongruous and overly dominant form of development. The proposal would disrupt the established rhythm of spacing between properties, create the appearance of a continuous facade, and fail to respect the character and appearance of the host dwelling and the surrounding street scene. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DMD14 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed rear dormer, by reason of its overall size extending over the existing and extended roof plane, and failure to retain any insets from the roof ridge, eaves or sides, would represent an overly dominant form of development which would be detrimental to the appearance of the host dwelling and would be out of keeping with the character of the immediately surrounding area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DMD 13 and DMD 37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
